// ------------------------------ Legal pages --------------------------------
function termsPage() {
  return pageShell({
    path: '/terms',
    title: 'Terms of Engagement | TheGo2Guys',
    desc: 'Terms of engagement for TheGo2Guys construction estimating services: scope, fees, payment, use of estimates, liability and confidentiality.',
    body: pageHero([['/', 'Home'], ['/terms', 'Terms of engagement']], 'Terms of engagement', 'These terms apply to every takeoff, estimate, bill of quantities and priced tender we prepare. Last updated 27 November 2026.') +
      `<section class="plain"><div class="container prose legal">
<h2>1. About us</h2>
<p>TheGo2Guys (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) provides construction estimating services from Liverpool to clients across the UK. You can contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@thego2guys.uk">hello@thego2guys.uk</a> or on <a href="tel:01516621274">0151 662 1274</a>. &ldquo;You&rdquo; means the person or business that instructs us.</p>
<h2>2. Scope of each instruction</h2>
<p>Before starting, we confirm in writing the documents we will work from, the service (takeoff, cost estimate, bill of quantities, tender pricing or specialist package), the fee and the delivery date. Work outside that scope, including re-pricing for revised drawings, is charged separately unless it is included in the service you ordered, such as the free re-price in the Tender Pack.</p>
<h2>3. Basis of our estimates</h2>
<p>Quantities are measured from the drawings, specifications and other information you supply, and rates reflect our assessment of current costs for the region and the date stated on the estimate. Every estimate lists the drawings and revisions used, and the assumptions, exclusions and provisional sums behind the figures.</p>
<p>An estimate is a forecast, not a quotation from a contractor or a guarantee of what the work will cost. Actual costs depend on the contractor appointed, ground and site conditions, design changes and market prices after the estimate date. We are not responsible for errors that arise from information that is missing, wrong or changed after we received it.</p>
<h2>4. What we need from you</h2>
<p>You are responsible for sending complete, current documents and telling us the return date of any tender. Delivery dates run from receipt of everything listed in the confirmed scope. If documents arrive late or change during the work, we will agree a revised date with you.</p>
<h2>5. Fees and payment</h2>
<p>Fees are fixed for the agreed scope and quoted excluding VAT where applicable. We invoice on delivery, and payment is due within 14 days of the invoice date by bank transfer. For instructions over &pound;500, or for new clients on larger packages, we may ask for 50% of the fee before starting. If an invoice is unpaid, we may charge statutory interest and compensation under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998 on business clients.</p>
<h2>6. Using our estimates</h2>
<p>Once our invoice is paid, you may use the estimate for the project it was prepared for. That includes sending it, or the client-facing PDF and bill of quantities, to your own client, subcontractors, suppliers, lender or design team for that project. It may not be used for a different project, resold, or published.</p>
<p>The estimate is prepared for you. Others who see it may not rely on it, and we accept no responsibility to anyone other than you. Copyright in our documents stays with us.</p>
<h2>7. Liability</h2>
<p>We prepare every estimate with reasonable skill and care. Our total liability to you for any instruction is limited to the fee paid for that instruction. We are not liable for loss of profit, loss of contract or other indirect loss, including losses from tender decisions, contract prices or material orders based on the estimate. Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or where the law does not allow it to be limited.</p>
<h2>8. Confidentiality</h2>
<p>Drawings, specifications, tender documents and project details you send are used only to prepare your estimate. We do not share them with anyone outside our own service providers without your consent, unless the law requires it. We are happy to sign a non-disclosure agreement before receiving tender documents.</p>
<h2>9. Cancellation</h2>
<p>You may cancel at any time before work starts at no charge. After that, you pay for the work done up to the date of cancellation, in proportion to the agreed fee.</p>
<p>If you are a homeowner instructing us as a consumer online or by phone, you also have 14 days from the date we confirm the instruction to cancel. If you ask us to start within those 14 days and then cancel, you pay for the work done up to that point. If the estimate has been delivered in full, the right to cancel no longer applies.</p>
<h2>10. Complaints</h2>
<p>If you are unhappy with an estimate, email us within 14 days of delivery explaining why. We will review it and reply within 5 working days, and correct any error at no charge.</p>
<h2>11. Law</h2>
<p>These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the courts of England and Wales have jurisdiction, except that a consumer living in Scotland or Northern Ireland may bring proceedings in their own courts.</p>
<h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>We may update these terms from time to time. The version on this page when we confirm your instruction applies to that instruction.</p>
</div></section>`
  });
}

function privacyPage() {
  return pageShell({
    path: '/privacy',
    title: 'Privacy Policy | TheGo2Guys',
    desc: 'How TheGo2Guys collects and uses your personal information.',
    body: pageHero([['/', 'Home'], ['/privacy', 'Privacy policy']], 'Privacy policy', 'Last updated 19 November 2026') +
      `<section class="plain"><div class="container prose legal"><h2>1. Who we are</h2><p>TheGo2Guys provides construction takeoff and estimating services to builders and contractors in the UK. We are the data controller for the personal information described here. Contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@thego2guys.uk">hello@thego2guys.uk</a> or on <a href="tel:01516621274">0151 662 1274</a>.</p><h2>2. What we collect</h2><p>Your name, email address, phone number and company name; details of the job you want priced; any drawings, plans, specifications or other documents you send us; and our correspondence with you. If you use a lead form on Facebook or Instagram, we receive only the information you submit in that form.</p><h2>3. How we use it</h2><p>To respond to your enquiry and contact you about your estimate, to prepare takeoffs, estimates and quotations, to provide our services, and to keep the business records the law requires. We will not send you marketing emails unless you have agreed to receive them, and you can opt out at any time.</p><h2>4. Our lawful basis</h2><p>We use your information to take steps at your request before entering into a contract (such as preparing an estimate), to perform a contract with you, for our legitimate interest in running our business, and to comply with legal obligations.</p><h2>5. Who we share it with</h2><p>We do not sell your information. We share it only with service providers that help us run the business, such as our email and file storage provider (Google Workspace), our website and form hosting providers (Cloudflare, FormSubmit), Google and Meta if you accept analytics cookies (see section 6), and Meta when you use a Facebook or Instagram lead form, or where the law requires it.</p><h2 id="cookies">6. Cookies and analytics</h2><p>The site works without cookies. If you click Accept on the cookie banner, we load Google Analytics, to count visits and see how people find the site, and the Meta Pixel, to measure whether our Facebook and Instagram adverts lead to enquiries. Both set cookies and share data about your visit with Google or Meta. If you click Reject, or ignore the banner, neither loads. Your choice is stored in your browser.</p><p><button type="button" class="btn-ghost" onclick="try{localStorage.removeItem('g2g_consent')}catch(e){};location.reload()">Change my cookie choice</button></p><h2>7. How long we keep it</h2><p>If you request an estimate but do not go on to work with us, we keep your details for up to 12 months and then delete them. If you become a client, we keep records for up to 6 years after our last job together, for accounting and legal purposes.</p><h2>8. Your rights</h2><p>Under UK data protection law you can ask to access, correct or delete your information, object to or restrict how we use it, and ask for a copy to be transferred to you. Email <a href="mailto:hello@thego2guys.uk">hello@thego2guys.uk</a> and we will respond within one month.</p><h2>9. Complaints</h2><p>If you are unhappy with how we have handled your information, please contact us first. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner&#39;s Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk</a> or on 0303 123 1113.</p><h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will always be on this page.</p></div></section>`
  });
}

